  "log": "r9-vectors-membership-log",
  "note": "The Portal's answers to reports (Auth/Portal, 2026-11-10). 200 confirms; a network error, a timeout, a 5xx, a 408, a 429 (after its Retry-After) or a 401 (after refreshing the station.report token) is retried with the same report_id and body; a final refusal (400, 404, 409 report_id_reused or invalid_state, 413, 415, any other 4xx) settles the report with an operator alert, and the reports waiting for it go once the others are settled. A 403 stops reporting under the Station's report client ID, with one alert: every report is held (none sent) while counting and reports go on, and a restart keeps the stop. A resume under the same ID (an operator fixed the token) clears the stop and keeps every report. A resume under another ID than the stop's is, as Atem reads Auth/Portal's \"start fresh\" (for Auth/Portal to confirm), another Station at Auth: the reports pending at that moment are dropped, each named in an alert and kept apart; nothing else changes, so the revocation reports on as usual. Here host-b's report is confirmed after a 401; host-c's is refused for good (409); the deadline's revoked{deadline_passed} waits for neither once both are settled, is retried after a 503, a 429 and a 408, and then gets a 403; host-d's late report is held, both go after a resume under the same ID; host-d's report gets a 403 again, and a resume under another ID drops it; host-e's later ack is reported under the new ID.",
